&lt;h1 data-hextra-search-id="pandafs-nanodfs-distributed-file-system"&gt;PandaFS (nanoDFS): Distributed File System&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/nanoDFS" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub Organization (nanoDFS)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/nanoDFS/Master" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master Node&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/nanoDFS/Slave" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Slave (Chunk Server)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/nanoDFS/client-sdk" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go Client SDK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/nanoDFS/p2p" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P2P Library&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PandaFS&lt;/strong&gt; (developed under the &lt;code&gt;nanoDFS&lt;/code&gt; organization) is a fault-tolerant, scalable, distributed file system modeled after the Google File System (GFS) architecture. Written in Go, it is engineered for high-bandwidth streaming reads and writes over large datasets across clusters of commodity hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="architectural-topology"&gt;Architectural Topology&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="architectural-topology"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#architectural-topology" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div role="img" aria-label="Diagram"&gt;
&lt;pre class="mermaid hx:mt-6"&gt;
flowchart TD
Client[nanoDFS Client SDK] &amp;lt;--&amp;gt;|1. Metadata / Chunk Locations| Master[nanoDFS Master Node]
subgraph StorageCluster [Distributed Chunk Servers]
Client &amp;lt;--&amp;gt;|2. Encrypted Chunk Stream| Chunk1[Slave Node 1 - Primary]
Chunk1 &amp;lt;--&amp;gt;|3. P2P Replication Pipeline| Chunk2[Slave Node 2 - Secondary]
Chunk2 &amp;lt;--&amp;gt;|4. P2P Replication Pipeline| Chunk3[Slave Node 3 - Tertiary]
end
Master &amp;lt;--&amp;gt;|Heartbeats &amp;amp; Block Reports| Chunk1
Master &amp;lt;--&amp;gt;|Heartbeats &amp;amp; Block Reports| Chunk2
Master &amp;lt;--&amp;gt;|Heartbeats &amp;amp; Block Reports| Chunk3
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="core-architecture-components"&gt;Core Architecture Components&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="core-architecture-components"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#core-architecture-components" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master Node (&lt;code&gt;nanoDFS/Master&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages the entire filesystem namespace, access control lists (ACL), and file-to-chunk mappings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitors chunk server health through periodic heartbeats and initiates automated re-replication upon node failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Never sits in the direct data transfer path, preventing bottlenecking on high-volume reads and writes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Slave / Chunk Servers (&lt;code&gt;nanoDFS/Slave&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stores 64MB fixed-size file chunks directly on local storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computes checksums per chunk to identify silent bit rot and data corruption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executes peer-to-peer chunk replication pipelines across secondary replicas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P2P Transport Protocol (&lt;code&gt;nanoDFS/p2p&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Custom low-level networking library maintaining persistent, bidirectional TCP connections between peer storage nodes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security &amp;amp; Cryptography&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client-Side Encryption&lt;/strong&gt;: Files are encrypted with symmetric keys (e.g. AES-256) on the client before being streamed to chunk servers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Token-Based Access Control&lt;/strong&gt;: Master issues time-bound cryptographic tokens for authorized chunk reads and writes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
